1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:26,520
Stay back, Homura! I got this!

2
00:00:26,520 --> 00:00:28,640
No way, Miss Kaname! I'll help!

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:59,980
Come to Kamihama...

4
00:00:59,980 --> 00:01:09,980
Where magical girls can be saved from their fate.

5
00:01:09,980 --> 00:01:12,780
Where magical girls can be saved from their fate.

6
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:14,380
Come to Kamehama.

7
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:17,540
Where magical girls can be saved from their fate.

8
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:19,020
Come to Kamehama.

9
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:22,060
We can be saved in Kamehama?

10
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:23,580
Who was that?

11
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:32,140
Oh no!

12
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:33,500
Madoka!

13
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:49,180
You came back just in time.

14
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:51,060
Thanks for saving us.

15
00:01:51,620 --> 00:01:52,740
Thank you, Miss Miki.

16
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:54,500
That was too close.

17
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:00,260
You idiot!

18
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:02,320
Are you trying to get Madoka killed?

19
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:04,240
If you're gonna pick a fight with a witch,

20
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:05,900
you should learn how to fight first.

21
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:07,880
I... I'm sorry.

22
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:10,160
It's not her fault, Sayaka.

23
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:12,240
I jumped in instead of waiting.

24
00:02:12,660 --> 00:02:14,720
All Homura was doing was trying to help.

25
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:19,500
Anyway, how'd it go with you?

26
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:21,560
Were you able to find Mami?

27
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:24,380
Yeah.

28
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:25,980
I found her.

29
00:02:26,340 --> 00:02:27,480
Oh, thank goodness.

30
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:30,340
Part of me wishes I didn't, though.

31
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:31,260
Huh?

32
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:34,360
She's like a different person.

33
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:37,380
Definitely not the Mami we used to know.

34
00:02:37,380 --> 00:02:43,520
Now what do we do?

35
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:45,840
What's wrong, Sayaka?

36
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:48,300
What are we gonna do?

37
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:53,160
All us magical girls are gonna end up turning into witches.

38
00:02:53,160 --> 00:03:01,620
A soul gem is born of hopes, dreams, wishes.

39
00:03:02,620 --> 00:03:05,120
It contains the soul of a magical girl.

40
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:09,240
In other words, this little thing is me.

41
00:03:10,900 --> 00:03:14,080
When it fills with despair and becomes dark and cloudy,

42
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:17,060
a magical girl transforms into a witch.

43
00:03:17,060 --> 00:03:21,840
Then, she spreads chaos, death, and destruction upon the world.

44
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:29,780
When a magical girl receives her wish,

45
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:32,300
she must accept this cursed existence

46
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:34,660
and join a fight that has no end.

47
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:39,400
At least, until she dies in battle against a witch.

48
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:42,380
Or, becomes a witch herself.

49
00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:46,000
That is the fate of a magical girl.

50
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:50,920
There's a rumor.

51
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:54,240
If a magical girl wants to be saved from her fate,

52
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:56,260
she should go to Kamehameha City.

53
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:59,460
I didn't know then what we needed saving from.

54
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:01,960
And now that I've been there

55
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:04,760
and found out the truth about us magical girls,

56
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:06,180
I do.

57
00:04:14,180 --> 00:04:15,120
No way.

58
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:16,660
It's not true.

59
00:04:17,180 --> 00:04:19,420
I didn't want to believe it either, but it's true.

60
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:21,580
Sooner or later, in the end,

61
00:04:21,860 --> 00:04:23,600
magical girls all turn into witches.

62
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:26,760
That means,

63
00:04:27,260 --> 00:04:29,100
when Kyuubi made those contracts with us,

64
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:29,960
he was lying?

65
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:31,660
That's rude.

66
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:33,500
I never lied to you.

67
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:34,820
Kyuubi!

68
00:04:35,180 --> 00:04:35,960
The deal was,

69
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:37,280
you'd be granted one wish,

70
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:38,440
no matter how impossible.

71
00:04:38,900 --> 00:04:40,440
And you'd become a magical girl

72
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:42,640
and assume the responsibilities of the job.

73
00:04:42,980 --> 00:04:43,980
That's a fair trade,

74
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,680
considering all the powers you got.

75
00:04:46,060 --> 00:04:47,980
Yeah, but you didn't say anything about us

76
00:04:47,980 --> 00:04:48,880
turning into witches!

77
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:50,400
Well, you didn't ask.

78
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:52,940
That's a pretty important detail to leave out!

79
00:04:53,260 --> 00:04:53,840
It's simple.

80
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:55,700
If you don't want to become witches,

81
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:58,120
just defeat them and take their grief seeds.

82
00:04:58,780 --> 00:05:01,600
As long as you keep purifying your soul gems with them,

83
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,260
why, you could live forever.

84
00:05:03,980 --> 00:05:04,540
Theoretically.

85
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:07,380
If you compare your lifespan and abilities

86
00:05:07,380 --> 00:05:08,600
to a normal human's,

87
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:10,280
it's not a bad trade at all.

88
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:12,220
It's a horrible trade.

89
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:13,500
The witches we fight,

90
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:15,460
they all used to be magical girls,

91
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:16,400
just like us!

92
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:17,120
That's right.

93
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:18,520
And just like you,

94
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:20,460
they all made contracts with me.

95
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:21,860
Now that they're witches,

96
00:05:22,180 --> 00:05:24,160
they torment the world with their suffering.

97
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:26,640
But you can release them from that fate

98
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:27,620
by defeating them!

99
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:30,380
Why would you do such an awful thing?

100
00:05:31,340 --> 00:05:33,380
When a soul gem finally burns out,

101
00:05:33,540 --> 00:05:34,720
it becomes a grief seed.

102
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:35,820
At that moment,

103
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:37,600
an incredible amount of energy

104
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:38,820
is released into the universe.

105
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:41,200
It's our job as incubators

106
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:43,540
to recover and redistribute that energy.

107
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:46,720
But what's the point of doing that?

108
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:48,200
If we didn't,

109
00:05:48,540 --> 00:05:50,600
entropy would expand unchecked

110
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:53,080
and the universe would eventually die out.

111
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:54,340
To survive,

112
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:56,240
the universe needs a source of energy

113
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:58,440
that isn't bound by the laws of thermodynamics.

114
00:05:59,220 --> 00:06:01,300
Your contribution is very important.

115
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:02,960
Now do you under-

116
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:05,520
I heard enough out of you!

117
00:06:05,840 --> 00:06:06,400
Sayaka!

118
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:08,320
That's what you get for tricking me!

119
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:09,380
And Mami!

120
00:06:09,740 --> 00:06:10,600
And Madoka!

121
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:14,620
That was mean.

122
00:06:15,180 --> 00:06:17,480
I was just trying to have a peaceful conversation.

123
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:19,200
Cubane!

124
00:06:19,220 --> 00:06:20,040
How in the heck?

125
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:22,640
Why is it that whenever you humans

126
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:24,700
come to regret a decision you made

127
00:06:24,700 --> 00:06:26,680
without fully understanding the situation,

128
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:28,480
you blame and hate others?

129
00:06:28,940 --> 00:06:30,940
Honestly, it's so baffling.

130
00:06:30,940 --> 00:06:32,160
I'll kill you!

131
00:06:41,660 --> 00:06:42,660
Miss Kaname.

132
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:48,760
You're not even a little freaked out over all this.

133
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,160
Why's that, new girl?

134
00:06:50,740 --> 00:06:52,380
You knew about this, didn't you?

135
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:53,180
What are you doing?

136
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:54,740
Calm down, Miss Miki.

137
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:56,540
Why didn't you tell us before?

138
00:06:56,860 --> 00:06:58,100
Or was it more fun for you

139
00:06:58,100 --> 00:06:59,700
sitting back and laughing at us?

140
00:06:59,700 --> 00:07:00,840
That's not true.

141
00:07:00,940 --> 00:07:02,000
She's not the enemy!

142
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:04,680
Stop trying to pick a bite with her already!

143
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:05,820
Miss Kaname!

144
00:07:06,540 --> 00:07:08,220
Being a magical girl is hard.

145
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:10,620
But we can't just drop everything now.

146
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:12,880
We have to stop this witch!

147
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:14,860
And we have to save Mami!

148
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:16,440
Save her?

149
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:17,900
You said yourself.

150
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:19,360
She's like a different person.

151
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,340
Yeah, I know what I said.

152
00:07:21,860 --> 00:07:22,640
She was.

153
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:26,380
We'll fall into despair, every one of us!

154
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:28,700
And then we'll become witches!

155
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:31,140
Can everyone really be saved?

156
00:07:31,500 --> 00:07:32,740
Do we even deserve to be?

157
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:35,580
Regardless, I will fulfill my duty!

158
00:07:36,060 --> 00:07:37,200
I promise that!

159
00:07:37,200 --> 00:07:40,160
I don't get it.

160
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:41,560
Why did she attack me?

161
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:43,940
Something happened to her.

162
00:07:44,160 --> 00:07:46,740
The way she was going on and on about saving us,

163
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:48,200
it's like she was possessed.

164
00:07:49,060 --> 00:07:49,860
That's it, then.

165
00:07:50,060 --> 00:07:51,140
If she tried to hurt you,

166
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:53,040
she definitely wasn't thinking straight.

167
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:54,220
She wasn't.

168
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:57,080
Then maybe she's been brainwashed by someone!

169
00:07:57,280 --> 00:07:58,200
Maybe by a witch!

170
00:07:58,280 --> 00:07:59,880
No, what else could it be?

171
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:01,880
But still...

172
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:04,720
What can we do about it?

173
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:06,340
I mean...

174
00:08:06,340 --> 00:08:07,480
Look at us.

175
00:08:07,740 --> 00:08:10,100
We can't even beat the witches here in this city.

176
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:12,220
And don't forget,

177
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:13,320
Walpurgisnacht.

178
00:08:13,620 --> 00:08:15,600
What are we supposed to do when she shows up?

179
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:19,860
She's the greatest, most evil witch ever.

180
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:22,320
We don't stand a chance against her.

181
00:08:23,040 --> 00:08:23,620
We never did.

182
00:08:26,740 --> 00:08:28,460
I don't want to end up a witch.

183
00:08:29,020 --> 00:08:29,880
More like Mommy.

184
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:41,240
I'm sorry.

185
00:08:42,020 --> 00:08:44,180
I thought I was doing the right thing.

186
00:08:44,820 --> 00:08:45,240
I know.

187
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:46,600
I get it.

188
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:49,460
You didn't want us falling into despair.

189
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:52,280
That's why you didn't say anything to us.

190
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:54,580
And you were right.

191
00:08:55,380 --> 00:08:56,600
You're not mad then?

192
00:08:58,160 --> 00:08:59,600
No, I'm not.

193
00:09:00,780 --> 00:09:02,200
Everything's gonna be okay.

194
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:26,960
I've repeated this time again and again with one goal.

195
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:29,020
To save Miss Kaname.

196
00:09:30,660 --> 00:09:32,060
I keep trying.

197
00:09:32,820 --> 00:09:33,140
Over.

198
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:34,620
And over.

199
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:34,660
And over.

200
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:36,240
And over.

201
00:09:36,240 --> 00:09:47,780
But this time,

202
00:09:47,780 --> 00:09:49,660
something different happened.

203
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:52,080
Maybe that means this time,

204
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:53,700
I can save her.

205
00:09:53,700 --> 00:10:01,740
I have to.

206
00:10:01,740 --> 00:10:10,780
Listen up, class.

207
00:10:10,920 --> 00:10:12,180
Whenever you address a woman,

208
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:14,380
saying Ms. rather than Miss or Mrs.

209
00:10:14,640 --> 00:10:17,800
helps you avoid getting their marital status wrong when you don't know it.

210
00:10:18,040 --> 00:10:19,500
However, calling your...

211
00:10:19,500 --> 00:10:20,460
Sayaka's absent.

212
00:10:20,460 --> 00:10:21,800
Let's everyone know you're single.

213
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:22,540
Komura too.

214
00:10:22,540 --> 00:10:27,720
You should find yourself a better role model.

215
00:10:28,540 --> 00:10:29,080
Not me.

216
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:30,820
I pretend to be cool.

217
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:32,520
When I'm scared or hurt,

218
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:35,640
I don't really have anyone I can turn to or talk to.

219
00:10:35,640 --> 00:10:38,560
All I can do is cry on my own.

220
00:10:39,260 --> 00:10:42,020
It's not fun being a magical girl.

221
00:10:45,380 --> 00:10:46,620
You were right, Mami.

222
00:10:47,460 --> 00:10:49,240
And now our team's coming apart.

223
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:58,040
If I can find out what's going on in Kami-hama,

224
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:01,580
maybe I can find a way to save Ms. Kaname.

225
00:11:07,280 --> 00:11:08,280
It's her again.

226
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:10,100
The witch we fought yesterday.

227
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:16,820
The witch's kiss.

228
00:11:16,820 --> 00:11:20,420
If she lures them into her labyrinth,

229
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:21,740
they're done for.

230
00:11:46,820 --> 00:11:50,500
That should hold them for a bit.

231
00:12:07,940 --> 00:12:09,720
I know what Miss Tomoe would do.

232
00:12:16,820 --> 00:12:21,620
Oh no.

233
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:23,320
Omura's on her own.

234
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:24,920
Hey!

235
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:25,660
Sayaka!

236
00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:28,540
Omura's fighting that witch from yesterday.

237
00:12:28,980 --> 00:12:29,660
By herself!

238
00:12:30,340 --> 00:12:30,580
What?

239
00:12:30,880 --> 00:12:31,760
That's crazy.

240
00:12:32,020 --> 00:12:32,900
Why would she do that?

241
00:12:33,520 --> 00:12:34,300
Who cares?

242
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:35,200
Where are you?

243
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:37,420
I'm busy.

244
00:12:39,100 --> 00:12:40,100
What do you mean?

245
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:42,840
I mean, I can't come help.

246
00:12:42,840 --> 00:12:46,720
What's the point of sacrificing yourself for others?

247
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:50,040
I can't do this anymore.

248
00:12:50,780 --> 00:12:51,500
No way.

249
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:53,680
I'm not brave like Mami.

250
00:12:54,380 --> 00:12:55,300
I'm scared.

251
00:12:55,820 --> 00:12:56,840
I'm scared too!

252
00:12:58,300 --> 00:12:59,580
It's totally normal.

253
00:13:00,300 --> 00:13:01,880
Mami told me she even gets scared.

254
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:02,500
Huh?

255
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:09,000
I've been thinking about that a lot and I realize as long as we stick together, we can take on anything.

256
00:13:10,480 --> 00:13:13,200
We need each other to survive as magical girls.

257
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:15,920
Odoka.

258
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:21,120
No matter how scary or painful or tough things get for us,

259
00:13:21,680 --> 00:13:24,180
we have each other to cry with and talk about it.

260
00:13:24,180 --> 00:13:27,940
We should never have become magical girls.

261
00:13:27,940 --> 00:13:31,400
But if we're together, I won't ever regret it!

262
00:13:47,460 --> 00:13:48,380
Please, Sayaka.

263
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:50,080
I really need your help here.

264
00:13:50,340 --> 00:13:51,020
I can't.

265
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:52,880
I'm not strong enough.

266
00:13:53,300 --> 00:13:54,120
Omura's in trouble.

267
00:13:54,660 --> 00:13:55,820
I'm heading in to save her.

268
00:13:55,820 --> 00:13:57,720
I can't do this alone.

269
00:13:57,940 --> 00:13:59,400
So come save me!

270
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:02,240
And then, the next time you get into trouble,

271
00:14:02,660 --> 00:14:03,880
Omura will come save you!

272
00:14:04,520 --> 00:14:05,880
You can handle it.

273
00:14:06,300 --> 00:14:07,180
You don't need me.

274
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:08,080
Alright then.

275
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:09,600
But if you don't come,

276
00:14:10,140 --> 00:14:11,740
I probably won't make it out alive!

277
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:13,360
Madoka?

278
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:14,260
Hey!

279
00:14:14,760 --> 00:14:15,120
Madoka!

280
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:19,760
What should I do?

281
00:14:20,440 --> 00:14:21,800
I'm totally useless.

282
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:25,960
What would you do, Mami?

283
00:14:27,940 --> 00:14:33,160
I'm sorry, Miss Kaname!

284
